cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use grounded-bio-mcp in research or other published work,
  please cite both this software and the upstream biomedical databases
  whose data it retrieves at query time.
title: "grounded-bio-mcp"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that grounds large-language-model
  answers in molecular biology by retrieving from primary databases
  (NCBI, UniProt, RCSB PDB, AlphaFold DB, EBI, ChEMBL, PubChem, Ensembl,
  Europe PMC, Reactome, STRING, NCBI BLAST, CRISPOR, ViennaRNA,
  Kazusa codon tables) instead of pattern-matching from training data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Devlin
    given-names: Devlin
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-04-25"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Actualbug2005/grounded-bio-mcp"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - large-language-models
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - hallucination-mitigation
  - clinical-genomics
  - drug-discovery
